{
  "title": "DubStarMooniCon",
  "children": [
    {
      "title": "Overview",
      "lines": [
        "Two oscillators with",
        "subharmonic dividers.",
        "",
        "VCO 1 is polyphonic",
        "(4 voices). VCO 2 is",
        "monophonic.",
        "",
        "Each oscillator has a",
        "core and two taps that",
        "divide it: 1:2, 1:3,",
        "1:4, 1:6, 1:8, 1:9, 1:12.",
        "",
        "No tuning. Every pitch",
        "control is a stepped",
        "selector, so there is",
        "nothing to set by ear."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Playing",
      "lines": [
        "Root page knobs:",
        "Cutoff, Resonance,",
        "VCO 1, Sub 1, Sub 2,",
        "VCO 2, Decay, Volume.",
        "",
        "Turn Sub 1 Level up to",
        "hear the divided tap a",
        "fifth below the core.",
        "",
        "The Filter page has the",
        "cutoff envelope. It is 0",
        "by default, so the filter",
        "starts still -- raise it",
        "and the cutoff moves with",
        "each note."
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Pages",
      "children": [
        {
          "title": "Osc 1 / Osc 2",
          "lines": [
            "Wave, the two Sub",
            "Freqs, Octave, and the",
            "three levels.",
            "",
            "Waves: Pulse, Pulse 25,",
            "Saw, Tri, Sine. Saw and",
            "both pulses are band-",
            "limited, so they stay",
            "clean at high pitch."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Filter",
          "lines": [
            "Cutoff, Resonance,",
            "Mode, Env Amount,",
            "Attack, Decay,",
            "VCA Attack, VCA Decay.",
            "",
            "Modes: Lowpass,",
            "Bandpass, Highpass.",
            "",
            "Resonance past about",
            "0.7 rings and sharpens",
            "the tone."
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Tune",
          "lines": [
            "The two octave offsets,",
            "Volume and Cutoff.",
            "",
            "Set VCO 2 an octave",
            "below VCO 1 to have the",
            "subharmonics land under",
            "the played note."
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Notes",
      "lines": [
        "There is no arpeggiator",
        "and no internal",
        "sequencer. Play it from",
        "the pads or from Move's",
        "own sequencer.",
        "",
        "The instrument can be",
        "quiet compared with some",
        "modules. That is its gain",
        "structure, not a fault:",
        "the levels are set so six",
        "overlapping signals",
        "cannot clip the filter.",
        "Raise Volume if you want",
        "more."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
